---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About — Baby Safety Site"
  description="What this site does, where its recall data comes from, and how often it updates."
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl p-4">
    <h1 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-bold">About this site</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-base-content/80">
      A small, fast page for checking whether baby and child products have been recalled.
    </p>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">What it does</h2>
      <p>
        It collects recalls of children's products so you can search them by product, brand, or
        store, or browse them by hazard. Each recall has its own page with a photo, the hazard, what
        to do (refund, repair, or replace), where it was sold, how to contact the company, and a
        link to the official notice.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Where the data comes from</h2>
      <p class="mb-3">
        Every recall shown here comes from the <a
          href="https://www.saferproducts.gov/RestWebServices/Recall"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="link link-primary"
          >U.S. Consumer Product Safety Commission<span class="sr-only">
            (opens in a new tab)</span
          ></a
        > public recalls API, filtered to children's products by keyword.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing is written or edited by hand — this site only reformats what the CPSC publishes. It
        is not affiliated with or endorsed by the CPSC. For anything official, follow the link on a
        recall page through to <span class="font-medium">cpsc.gov</span>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">How current it is</h2>
      <p>
        New recalls are collected from the CPSC once a day and the site is republished straight
        after, so a recall announced today should appear here by tomorrow. The home page shows when
        the data was last updated. For the very latest announcements, check <a
          href="https://www.cpsc.gov/Recalls"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="link link-primary"
          >cpsc.gov/Recalls<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="alert alert-warning">
      <span>
        This site is an informational convenience, not a safety guarantee. An item not appearing
        here does not mean it has not been recalled.
      </span>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
